<title>USA: CalMat Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>CalMat Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>CALMAT EARNINGS REPORT</p>
<p>(unaudited, amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     1996		1995</p>
<p>Quarter Ended December 31:</p>
<p> Revenues				     $101,997	 $104,320</p>
<p> Net Income (loss)  (a)			  298	 (26,709)</p>
<p>Per Share Data:</p>
<p> Net Income (loss) (a)			  0.01	   (1.15)</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares		    23,274	   23,172</p>
<p>Twelve Months Ended December 31:</p>
<p> Revenues					407,895	  378,182</p>
<p> Net Income (loss) (a), (b)		  9,334	 (21,371)</p>
<p>Per Share Data:</p>
<p> Net Income (loss) (a), (b)		   0.40	   (0.92)</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares		    23,245	   23,176</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) The 1995 amounts include a charge of $26.5 million, or $1.14 per share, to adopt the accounting standard for impairment of long-lived assets (SFAS 121).</p>
<p>(b) The 1995 amounts include an after-tax charge of $1.2 million, or $0.05 per share, related to a consolidation of certain construction materials operations.</p>
</text>
